Catalog data sources
--------------------

monkeypatchlist's runtime catalog (catalog/catalog.json) is generated from the
upstream packages below, at the exact versions recorded in the catalog's
metadata.upstream, together with curated overlays that are part of monkeypatchlist.
The catalog records the names, owners and shapes of web platform and
ECMAScript APIs that these sources define.

  @webref/idl (W3C webref)
    https://github.com/w3c/webref
    Web IDL extracted from the specifications of the web platform.
    Package license: MIT.
    The IDL comes from specifications published by the W3C, the WHATWG and
    other groups, each under its own license. WHATWG Living Standards are
    licensed under the Creative Commons Attribution 4.0 International License
    (CC BY 4.0), copyright WHATWG (Apple, Google, Mozilla, Microsoft). W3C
    specifications are copyright World Wide Web Consortium; code components
    such as IDL are available under the W3C Software and Document License.

  webidl2
    https://github.com/w3c/webidl2.js
    The Web IDL parser the generator reads @webref/idl with.
    License: MIT (its LICENSE file; its package.json declares W3C, the W3C
    Software and Document License). Copyright (c) 2014 Robin Berjon.

  @tc39/ecma262-biblio and @tc39/ecma402-biblio
    https://github.com/tc39/ecma262 and https://github.com/tc39/ecma402
    The ECMA-262 (ECMAScript) and ECMA-402 (Internationalization API)
    specification biblios, for the ECMAScript intrinsics.
    Licensed under Ecma International TC39's Intellectual Property Policy:
    natural language text under the alternative copyright notice of the Ecma
    text copyright policy, and source code under the Ecma International Policy
    on Submission, Inclusion and Licensing of Software. Copyright Ecma
    International.

The catalog generator also cross-checks the catalog against two sources that
never change it, at exact-pinned versions:

  ses (Endo) src/permits.js
    https://github.com/endojs/endo
    License: Apache-2.0. Copyright Endo Contributors.

  @mdn/browser-compat-data
    https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data
    License: CC0-1.0. Data from MDN Web Docs and its contributors.


Runtime dependencies
--------------------

monkeypatchlist's runtime dependencies are installed separately by the package
manager, under their own licenses (MIT, BSD-2-Clause and BSD-3-Clause), and
none of their code is bundled into this package. In the source repository,
`npm run licenses:check` lists them.
